+# 001 - Deduplicate Training Candidates
+
+> **Gate discipline:** One gate → do work → check box → next gate.
+> **Closing a gate:** check the box, append your outcome. Never replace the original text.
+
+## Status
+pending
+
+## Intent
+Training rounds waste LLM budget on duplicate candidates. The same article crossposted to multiple subreddits appears multiple times in each batch. Implement two dedup methods, evaluate them against labeled ground truth, find optimal thresholds, pick the better default, and justify your choice with precision/recall numbers.
+
+## Why
+Observed during training: round 2 had ~20 unique items out of 40 — half the batch was duplicates. Each LLM classification costs tokens. Deduplication would double the effective diversity per round. Two methods because embedding similarity catches semantic duplicates while n-gram overlap catches textual duplicates — different failure modes. We need to know which works better for our data.
+
