+
+## Design Phase
+
+### Understand
+- [ ] Read the training loop in `semlabel.py`. Where are candidates selected? How does the embedding work? Where would deduplication fit?
+- [ ] Understand the two dedup approaches: (1) dot product on pre-computed normalized embeddings, (2) char 3-gram cosine similarity via sklearn TfidfVectorizer sparse dot product (TF-IDF vectors are L2-normalized, so dot product = cosine). What are the trade-offs?
+- [ ] Read `fixtures/golden_duplicates.json` — understand the labeled clusters and duplicate types (exact vs near).
+- [ ] What does "done" look like? How will you verify both methods work?
+
+### Structure
+- [ ] Plan your approach. What module(s) to create? How to wire the `--dedup-method` flag? How will you evaluate against golden duplicates?
+
+### Reflection Gates
+- [ ] Test strategy: what are you testing and how? (point tests for specific behavior, property tests via `hypothesis` for invariants on transformations/parsers/arithmetic)
